                        "content": "Zidovudine has been prescribed for a client, and the nurse provides instructions to the client about expected effects with this medication. Which statement by the client indicates the need for further instruction?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "a0f7d178f7b728b8bba7ef20ddeca62d",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Evaluating 评价",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nHuman immunodeficiency virus (HIV) can cause acquired immunodeficiency syndrome, which is a viral disease that destroys T cells, thereby increasing susceptibility to infection and malignancy. Zidovudine is a nucleoside reverse transcriptase inhibitor that is used in combination with other retroviral agents to treat human immunodeficiency virus (HIV) infection. Diarrhea is an occasional side effect of the medication and does not warrant notification of the primary health care provider. Monitoring temperature, knowing that nausea can occur, and understanding the need for periodic blood tests reflect an understanding of the medication instructions.",
                        "id": "097aec77c8c04a879e2fd198ae4d424b",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "5b8cc229efea4fdf89234070b6b4df96",
                                "content": "Monitoring blood glucose levels for elevation"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "a91d68174feb412fa52f4dbbab6b2a8d",
                                "content": "Administering the medication on an empty stomach only"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "f490a24b566d4edfaa799d4bd9a38f79",
                                "content": "Applying pressure to venipuncture sites for at least 1 minute"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "dea6144fdb2d4cbbbc4e9c43b23ab5af",
                                "content": "Providing the client with a soft toothbrush and an electric razor"
                            }
                        ],
