                        "version": 0,
                        "content": "A client is receiving tacrolimus to prevent organ rejection. Which is a nursing consideration associated with this medication?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "11797937e327eb6d913faa80427c566b",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Analyzing 分析",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nTacrolimus is an immunosuppressant and is an alternative to cyclosporine for prevention of organ rejection in clients receiving an organ transplant. It would never be given with cyclosporine because of its toxic effects on the kidney. This medication will cause hyperglycemia (not hypoglycemia). Grapefruit juice can increase tacrolimus levels, so it would be avoided to prevent toxicity. Tacrolimus suppresses the bone marrow, so it can cause anemia, thrombocytopenia, and neutropenia.",
                        "id": "0c5004c9f9e04ddaafa35298f06093e1",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "69f4463544914d95ac42fc16edecca7e",
                                "content": "Monitoring the leukocyte count for 2 days after the infusion"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "8908b98c006d48e5b14ef647b58877d7",
                                "content": "Checking the frequency and consistency of bowel movements"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "636c9167b86f4b198b93cb74de0d3a97",
                                "content": "Checking serum liver enzyme levels before and after the infusion"
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "ced502cc684a46b29541aff8620c4ae0",
                                "content": "Carrying out a Hematest on gastric fluids after the infusion is completed"
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "69f4463544914d95ac42fc16edecca7e",
                                    "content": "Monitoring the leukocyte count for 2 days after the infusion"
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "1",
