                        "content": "A client with Crohn's disease is scheduled to receive an infusion of infliximab. What intervention by the nurse will determine the effectiveness of treatment?",
                        "subjectId": "ad5ab04c79144c0ea9b83385308c3b1d",
                        "difficultyIds": "a0f7d178f7b728b8bba7ef20ddeca62d",
                        "difficulty": "考试范围-Evaluating 评价",
                        "textAnalysis": "Rationale:\nThe principal manifestations of Crohn's disease are diarrhea and abdominal pain. Infliximab is an immunomodulator that reduces the degree of inflammation in the colon, thereby reducing the diarrhea. Options 1, 3, and 4 are unrelated to this medication.",
                        "id": "0f1a5604ea8b4029a24c5a9acd87bb53",
                        "mark": "0",
                        "collectionState": "0"
                    },
                    {
                        "optionList": [
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "984c5ef998de4f49a14a4d934d699ac7",
                                "content": "It is classified as a narrow-spectrum antibiotic."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "634729a4580441acbe421145423da7b1",
                                "content": "It is identified as safe for use during pregnancy."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "0",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "63cd48a0cd9c4922bf0f28561247ac55",
                                "content": "It is used to treat a wide variety of disease processes."
                            },
                            {
                                "isRight": "1",
                                "userAnswer": "",
                                "isSelected": "0",
                                "id": "a19deabbf1754a47a964b75bf8211cdb",
                                "content": "It is contraindicated in children younger than 8 years of age."
                            }
                        ],
                        "extJson": {
                            "optionList": [
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "984c5ef998de4f49a14a4d934d699ac7",
                                    "content": "It is classified as a narrow-spectrum antibiotic."
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "634729a4580441acbe421145423da7b1",
                                    "content": "It is identified as safe for use during pregnancy."
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "0",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "63cd48a0cd9c4922bf0f28561247ac55",
                                    "content": "It is used to treat a wide variety of disease processes."
                                },
                                {
                                    "isRight": "1",
                                    "userAnswer": "",
                                    "isSelected": "0",
                                    "id": "a19deabbf1754a47a964b75bf8211cdb",
                                    "content": "It is contraindicated in children younger than 8 years of age."
                                }
                            ]
                        },
